# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL-ONLY: everything below stays on the maintainer's machine and is kept
# out of the published repository (github.com/Kohulan/Orthonym-Web), which was
# rewritten on 2026-09-07 so none of it appears in any commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The engine, and everything derived from it. `backend/vendor/` used to be
# tracked in full; it is not, because scripts/vendor-orthonym.sh copies ALL
# of it -- engine source, OPSIN grammar resources, the opsin-cli and
# centres-cli jars -- out of a checkout of Orthonym, which is a private
# repository. Publishing the vendored snapshot would publish the engine.
# A fresh clone populates this directory with that script; see README.
backend/vendor/orthonym/
# `/*`, not `/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is
# excluded, so the directory has to stay visible and its entries excluded
# individually for the negation below to bite.
backend/vendor/opsin-resources/*
# ...with ONE exception, tracked deliberately. centres-cli-1.5.jar is a local
# Maven build from an unreleased commit (develop @ d4b3cf0, pom 1.5-SNAPSHOT),
# so unlike the CDK and opsin-cli jars it cannot be downloaded -- the newest
# release at github.com/SiMolecule/centres is 1.2.1. Shipping it keeps the CIP
# stereo-descriptor path reproducible from a clone.
#
# Redistribution is permitted: upstream's LICENSE says BSD-2-Clause (which is
# also what GitHub reports for the repo) while its pom says LGPL-3.0, and the
# NOTICE treats the stricter reading as binding. Either way the jar is
# redistributed unmodified, which both licences allow, as do the terms of the
# CDK (LGPL-2.1) and javax.vecmath (GPLv2 + Classpath) it shades in. The
# notice travels with it in backend/vendor/orthonym/NOTICE -- which does NOT
# ship -- so /terms carries the same statement on the site itself.
#
# 1.2.1 was measured as a drop-in on 2026-09-07: same Main-Class, and
# byte-identical labels across 10 hard cases (hexitol, pseudo-asymmetric
# 2s/5s, an allene, a bridged bicyclic, tetrasubstituted E/Z, tartaric acid).
# Swapping to the downloadable release is therefore viable later; run
# Orthonym's tests/integration/test_cip_validation.py first, because 10
# molecules is a spot-check and the 279/290 figure comes from 290.
!backend/vendor/opsin-resources/centres-cli-1.5.jar
# The CDK jar is the one vendored artifact with a public source, so the
# backend Dockerfile downloads it (pinned version, checked against the
# SHA-256 in backend/vendor/cdk/NOTICE, which IS tracked).
backend/vendor/cdk/*.jar

